			"verticalAlign": "middle",
			"containerId": "PPWkVhyVEGH45PGsPA2V8",
			"originalText": "+----------------------+----------------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------+\n| Feature              | Polling                                            | WebSocket                                         |\n+----------------------+----------------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------+\n| Definition           | Client repeatedly asks the server for updates      | Persistent two-way client-server connection       |\n+----------------------+----------------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------+\n| Working              | Sends HTTP requests at fixed time intervals        | Keeps one connection open for live messages       |\n+----------------------+----------------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------+\n| Communication        | Client initiates every request                     | Client and server can send messages anytime       |\n+----------------------+----------------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------+\n| Connection           | Creates or reuses an HTTP connection per poll      | Maintains one long-lived connection               |\n+----------------------+----------------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------+\n| Direction            | Primarily request-response communication           | Full-duplex bidirectional communication           |\n+----------------------+----------------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------+\n| Latency              | Depends on the polling interval                    | Very low after the connection is established      |\n+----------------------+----------------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------+\n| Network overhead     | Repeated requests add headers and empty responses  | Low overhead after the initial handshake          |\n+----------------------+----------------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------+\n| Scalability          | Frequent polling can increase server load          | Many open connections require careful management  |\n+----------------------+----------------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------+\n| Missed updates       | Updates wait until the next polling request        | Updates can be pushed immediately                 |\n+----------------------+----------------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------+\n| Failure handling     | Each new request can recover independently         | Requires reconnect and connection-state logic     |\n+----------------------+----------------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------+\n| Infrastructure       | Works easily with HTTP servers and proxies         | Needs WebSocket-aware servers and proxies         |\n+----------------------+----------------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------+\n| Key difference       | Checks periodically whether new data exists        | Server pushes data as soon as it is available     |\n+----------------------+----------------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------+\n| Advantages           | Simple, stateless, compatible, and easy to cache   | Real-time, efficient, and bidirectional           |\n+----------------------+----------------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------+\n| Disadvantages        | Higher latency, wasted requests, and more traffic  | More complex connection and scaling management    |\n+----------------------+--------------------------